{
  "dom_id": "step-e14381",
  "name": "Example: Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence",
  "problem": "What is the $8$th term of the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n4, \\: 7, \\: 10, \\: 13, \\: 16, \\: \\ldots\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14203588/assets/ac878a3d258fa19641d983863580af953bbea593b49bffff16f2f09eb7b6ab2d.png)\n\nWe notice that the sequence is an arithmetic sequence with a common difference of \n\n$$\nd=7-4=3.\n$$\n\nSo, we can calculate each term in the sequence by adding $3$ to the previous term. \n\nWe will continue listing terms of the sequence until we get to the $8$th term. Listing the terms up to the $8$th term, we have:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14203588/assets/e536739b28db7d0f221967ce8729eee502a29f80caec8e1c39f61a9cfe4a6459.png)\n\nTherefore, the $8$th term is $25.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
